**PASS.** All 9 brief verification points hold in the current file:

- 209 lines (within 207–209 range) — x86_emit.oo end-to-end
- 22 arms in chain — x86_emit.oo:93–205 (fold at 93 + 21 match_* arms)
- 5-shape refuse gate — x86_emit.oo:76–84
- Silent fall-through fixed — x86_emit.oo:90 (Err exits hard)
- Tier 5 #24 Turn 1 shim — x86_emit.oo:87–91
- 4-element header (Title, Logline, Setup, Beats) — x86_emit.oo:1–12
- All 29 imports valid (each file exists in ooda/oodac/) — x86_emit.oo:16–44
- No dead imports (`x86_emit_list.oo` and `x86_emit_diag.oo` removed) — x86_emit.oo:16–44
- 3 new gates at top: contract (48–57), secret (63–72), shape (73–84)

The only discrepancy is the brief's mention of a "diag" gate. The actual 3rd gate is the 5-shape refuse gate, consistent with the post-fix audit and the file's own comment. The "diag" reference is a brief-side typo and does not affect the post-fix state of the code.

The file is in clean post-fix state and ready for the next pass.
